He clambered to shore and flagged down a passing car for help. When recalling these events to police that night, Robert described everything as having happened so quickly, just a big blur. Both policemen noted that Robert seemed calm when telling his story. The only time he coughed was when he described the fit he'd had while driving. Robert didn't ask whether his children had been found. And Smith said carefully, Mate, do you realise that the children didn't make it out of the car?
他艰难地爬上岸，拦下一辆过往的汽车寻求帮助。当晚向警方回忆这些事件时，罗伯特形容一切发生得太快，只是一片模糊。两名警察都注意到罗伯特在讲述他的故事时显得很平静。他唯一咳嗽的时候是他描述开车时发作的那一次。罗伯特没有询问是否找到了他的孩子们。史密斯警长小心翼翼地说道：“老兄，你意识到孩子们没能从车里出来吗？”

